|term[progressive-routing]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss Per-hop ownership of resolution; quietly generates most of the machinery.
  |designation progressive-routing
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-locations-and-paths
    :anchor progressive-routing
    :projection paraphrase
    Paths are resolved progressively: each intermediate location is in charge of routing from there. Corollaries: re-binding one intermediate re-routes every path through it; a default at an intermediate is a routing choice; resolution as a whole is the composite of these per-hop responsibilities.
  |rel :kind performed-by :to @resolution-engine
  |marker
    DNS delegation, mount points, symlinks, import maps — any place one hop owns the next.
